Two example features (Biometric + SMS OTP login, and Shopping Cart),
then all the cross-cutting concerns (coverage, network, performance, security, telemetry, tooling, and exit criteria).
_____________________________________________________________________
0) Scope & Assumptions

Platforms: iOS (16–18), Android (12–15); phones first, sanity on tablets.

Builds: Debug + Release; Feature flags for OTP and biometrics.

Envs: Staging mirrors prod auth flows (rate limits, OTP TTL, fraud checks); test accounts seeded.

1) Risk-Based Prioritization (what I’d say up front)

Highest risk: authentication correctness & abuse prevention (lockouts, replay, rate-limits), payment/price integrity, session management.

Medium: UX friction, device/OS fragmentation, flakiness from network timing.

Lower: cosmetic issues that don’t block core flows.
_____________________________________________________________________

A) Login with Biometric + SMS OTP
A1) Functional Test Design (happy paths first)

First-time login (no biometric enrolled)

Enter valid user + password → prompt for SMS OTP → enter valid OTP → success → optional “Enable FaceID/TouchID” prompt → accept → relaunch app → biometric unlock succeeds.

Returning user (biometric enrolled)

Cold start → biometric prompt → success → lands on home.

Fallback path

Biometric fails/unavailable → fallback to password + OTP → success.

Negative & Edge Cases (high-value)

OTP wrong (single digit wrong; completely wrong; expired TTL).

OTP resent: enforce cooldown, last-code-wins.

OTP delivery failures: show retry guidance; “call me” option if supported.

Rate limiting: too many OTP requests → friendly throttle message; too many failed OTP entries → temporary lockout; verify unlock timer.

Device time skew (>2 mins): OTP validation behavior, error copy.

Biometric permutations:

User cancels biometric sheet; retries once; locks out after N failed attempts → fallback works.

Device with multiple biometrics enrolled (two faces/fingers).

Biometric disabled in OS settings between sessions.

Session cases:

Token expiry on background → foreground requires re-auth.

Logout clears tokens & cached screens.

Accessibility:

Biometric & OTP screens fully navigable via VoiceOver/TalkBack; focus order; semantics on code inputs; sufficient contrast.

Localization:

OTP numbers and LTR/RTL layouts (Arabic/Hebrew) render correctly; no truncation.
